            "number": 1576,
            "title": "fix(tracing): mount nested apps passed to `use()`",
            "body": "`tracingPlugin` breaks mounting nested apps with `use()`. The plugin's `use()` override wraps its argument with `wrapMiddleware()` before the original `use()` gets to inspect it. `use()` dispatches non-function inputs (an H3 app or any other mountable object) to `mount()` — but after the wrapper, the input is a function, so:\n\n- the nested app is never mounted: its routes silently 404,\n- a middleware that calls the wrapped app as a function is registered instead, so hitting the base path exactly (e.g. `/api`) throws a `TypeError` (500).\n\n`use(route, handler: Middleware | H3, opts?)` is a public documented signature, and the plugin's `mount()` override already propagates tracing to mounted apps — so `app.use(\"/api\", app2)` should behave exactly like `app.mount(\"/api\", app2)`. The existing tracing tests cover `.mount()` and function middlewares but never the mountable `use()` shape, which is how this slipped through.\n\nThe fix passes non-function inputs through to the original `use()` unwrapped, in both call shapes. The `mount()` override then takes over and the nested app is traced like any other mount.\n\nTests: new regression test `mounts a nested app passed to `use()`\"` mounts a nested app with `t.app.use(\"/api\", nestedApp)` on the tracing-enabled matrix app and asserts the route responds 200 with the right body and shows up in the traced route events. It fails on `main` (404) and passes with this change. `test/tracing.test.ts` is 54/54 on both web and node targets; `tsc --noEmit`, `oxlint` and `oxfmt --check` are clean. Full suite: 3 failures (`test/utils.test.ts`, `test/unit/event.test.ts`, `test/unit/route-normalize.test.ts`) — all three also fail on unmodified `main`, unrelated to this change.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Nested H3 apps mounted with `use()` now remain mountable, and tracing events include the mounted route’s full path.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
